{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c8b5ada2-00cf-46f8-a97c-f9793e18383d",
    "name": "Harmattan Wallet API v1",
    "description": "Frontend integration contract for the Operation Borderless wallet sandbox.\n\nAmounts and rates are decimal strings. Deposit, swap execution, and transfer require an `Idempotency-Key`. Reuse the same key only when retrying the exact same body; a changed body with that key returns `409`.\n\nThe deposit amount-window and transfer recipient-velocity checks are informational. They may log or softly pace a request, but they never reject an otherwise valid operation.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Check API health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
            "description": "Checks that the API can reach PostgreSQL.\n\n**200 fields:** `status`, `database`, `timestamp`.\n\n**503:** `DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE`.\n\nExample: `{ \"status\": \"ok\", \"database\": \"up\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-29T15:00:00.000Z\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('API is healthy', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Wallet creation and balances",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create sender wallet",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"amara.{{$timestamp}}@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets",
            "description": "Creates one wallet with five zero balances. Supply email, mobile, or both.\n\n**201 fields:** `id`, `email`, `mobile`, `balances`, `totalUsdEquivalent`, `createdAt`.\n\n**400:** invalid or missing identifier. **409:** email/mobile already used.\n\nExample balances: `{ \"cNGN\": \"0.00000000\", \"cGHS\": \"0.00000000\", \"cXAF\": \"0.00000000\", \"USDx\": \"0.00000000\", \"EURx\": \"0.00000000\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Wallet created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const wallet = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', wallet.id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create receiver wallet",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"kwame.{{$timestamp}}@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets",
            "description": "Creates the second wallet used in the transfer example. The response shape and errors match Create sender wallet."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Receiver wallet created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const wallet = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('receiverWalletId', wallet.id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get wallet balances",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{walletId}}",
            "description": "Returns all five balances and their combined USDx value from one FX snapshot.\n\n**200 fields:** wallet identity, `balances`, `totalUsdEquivalent`, and `valuation` metadata.\n\n**404:** `WALLET_NOT_FOUND`. **503:** FX or database unavailable.\n\nExample: `{ \"balances\": { \"cNGN\": \"1600.00000000\", \"cGHS\": \"0.00000000\", \"cXAF\": \"0.00000000\", \"USDx\": \"0.00000000\", \"EURx\": \"0.00000000\" }, \"totalUsdEquivalent\": \"1.00000000\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Wallet balances returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const wallet = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', wallet.id);",
                  "  if (wallet.valuation && wallet.valuation.snapshotId) pm.collectionVariables.set('fxSnapshotId', wallet.valuation.snapshotId);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Deposits",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Deposit simulated funds",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{depositIdempotencyKey}}",
                "description": "Reuse this key only to retry this exact body."
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currency\": \"cNGN\",\n  \"amount\": \"1600.00\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{walletId}}/deposits",
            "description": "Immediately credits one balance and writes a deposit transaction.\n\nTwo same-wallet, same-amount deposits with different keys are both valid. The soft amount-window signal never blocks them.\n\n**201 fields:** `transaction` and resulting `balance`. **400:** validation or missing key. **404:** wallet missing. **409:** key reused with another body.\n\nExample balance: `{ \"walletId\": \"...\", \"currency\": \"cNGN\", \"available\": \"1600.00000000\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Deposit accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const result = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', result.balance.walletId);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', result.transaction.id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Swaps",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create swap quote",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sourceCurrency\": \"cNGN\",\n  \"destinationCurrency\": \"USDx\",\n  \"sourceAmount\": \"1600.00\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{walletId}}/swaps/quotes",
            "description": "Creates a short-lived server quote. Execute it before `expiresAt`.\n\n**201 fields:** `quoteId`, source/destination currencies and amounts, `quotedRate`, `rateAsOf`, `expiresAt`.\n\n**400:** invalid/same currency. **404:** wallet missing. **422:** per-currency cap or rounded-to-zero result. **503:** FX unavailable.\n\nExample: `{ \"quoteId\": \"...\", \"sourceAmount\": \"1600.00000000\", \"destinationAmount\": \"1.00000000\", \"quotedRate\": \"0.000625000000000000\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Quote created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const quote = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('quoteId', quote.quoteId);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', quote.walletId);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Execute quoted swap",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{swapIdempotencyKey}}",
                "description": "Reuse this key and quoteId to safely retry."
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"quoteId\": \"{{quoteId}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{walletId}}/swaps",
            "description": "Atomically debits the source balance and credits the destination balance using the execution rate.\n\n**201 fields:** `transaction` and both resulting balances. **409:** `FX_QUOTE_EXPIRED`, `FX_RATE_MOVED`, or changed body for the key. **422:** insufficient funds/cap. **503:** FX unavailable.\n\nA rate move over 50 basis points rejects and rolls back the provisional key so a retry is safe."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Swap executed', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const transaction = pm.response.json().transaction;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', transaction.id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', transaction.senderWalletId);",
                  "  if (transaction.fxSnapshotId) pm.collectionVariables.set('fxSnapshotId', transaction.fxSnapshotId);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Transfers",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Transfer between wallets",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{transferIdempotencyKey}}",
                "description": "Reuse only for an exact retry."
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"senderWalletId\": \"{{walletId}}\",\n  \"receiverWalletId\": \"{{receiverWalletId}}\",\n  \"sourceCurrency\": \"USDx\",\n  \"destinationCurrency\": \"cGHS\",\n  \"sourceAmount\": \"0.50\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/transfers",
            "description": "Atomically debits the sender and credits the receiver. Different currencies convert automatically.\n\nRecipient-velocity detection is informational and never returns `429` by itself.\n\n**201 fields:** `transaction`, `senderBalance`, `receiverBalance`. **400:** validation/missing key. **404:** either wallet missing. **409:** key conflict. **422:** insufficient funds/rounded-to-zero. **503:** FX unavailable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Transfer completed', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  const transaction = pm.response.json().transaction;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', transaction.id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', transaction.senderWalletId);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('receiverWalletId', transaction.receiverWalletId);",
                  "  if (transaction.fxSnapshotId) pm.collectionVariables.set('fxSnapshotId', transaction.fxSnapshotId);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Transaction history",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List wallet transactions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/wallets/{{walletId}}/transactions?limit=20",
            "description": "Lists deposits, swaps, sent transfers, and received transfers newest first.\n\nOptional query fields: `type` (`DEPOSIT`, `SWAP`, `TRANSFER`), `currency`, `cursor`, and `limit` (1-100, default 20).\n\n**200 fields:** `data` transaction array and `pageInfo` with `hasNextPage` and `nextCursor`. Empty history is `{ \"data\": [], \"pageInfo\": { \"hasNextPage\": false, \"nextCursor\": null } }`.\n\n**400:** invalid filter/cursor. **404:** wallet missing."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('History returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const history = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (history.data && history.data.length > 0) pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', history.data[0].id);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('cursor', history.pageInfo && history.pageInfo.nextCursor ? history.pageInfo.nextCursor : '');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Single transaction lookup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get transaction by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/transactions/{{transactionId}}",
            "description": "Returns one immutable operation.\n\n**200 fields:** `id`, `type`, sender/receiver wallet IDs, source/destination amount and currency, applied rate, rate timestamp/source, FX snapshot ID, and transaction timestamp.\n\n**404:** `TRANSACTION_NOT_FOUND`.\n\nExample: `{ \"type\": \"transfer\", \"sourceAmount\": \"0.50000000\", \"sourceCurrency\": \"USDx\", \"destinationAmount\": \"7.75000000\", \"destinationCurrency\": \"cGHS\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Transaction returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const transaction = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', transaction.id);",
                  "  if (transaction.senderWalletId) pm.collectionVariables.set('walletId', transaction.senderWalletId);",
                  "  if (transaction.receiverWalletId) pm.collectionVariables.set('receiverWalletId', transaction.receiverWalletId);",
                  "  if (transaction.fxSnapshotId) pm.collectionVariables.set('fxSnapshotId', transaction.fxSnapshotId);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Rates",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get all conversion rates",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/rates",
            "description": "Returns the complete 5-by-5 rate matrix: 25 decimal-string rates including identity rates of 1.\n\n**200 fields:** `snapshotId`, `source`, `provider`, `rateAsOf`, `fetchedAt`, `freshness`, `rates`, and optional `lastLive` fallback metadata.\n\n**503:** `FX_UNAVAILABLE` or database unavailable.\n\nExample rate: `{ \"base\": \"cNGN\", \"quote\": \"USDx\", \"rate\": \"0.000625000000000000\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('All 25 rates returned', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); pm.expect(pm.response.json().rates).to.have.length(25); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) pm.collectionVariables.set('fxSnapshotId', pm.response.json().snapshotId);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "walletId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "receiverWalletId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "quoteId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "transactionId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "fxSnapshotId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "cursor", "value": "" },
    { "key": "depositIdempotencyKey", "value": "postman-deposit-0001" },
    { "key": "swapIdempotencyKey", "value": "postman-swap-0001" },
    { "key": "transferIdempotencyKey", "value": "postman-transfer-0001" }
  ]
}
